    "view_invariant_remnant": 693,
    "so": "The overlay is view-dependent, because its bar length encodes each view's metres-per-pixel. Intersecting all nine frames keeps only the remnant and leaves the rest of the label in the image, where it goes on pinning the bounding box. Within one view the band is identical across reconstructions, which is the invariance that isolates it."
